{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "CodeKavach",
          "version": "0.1.0.dev0",
          "semanticVersion": "0.1.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/jatinsingh1603/Source-Code-Review-Tool-TIET",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "iac.actions.pull-request-target-checkout",
              "name": "InclusionOfFunctionalityFromUntrustedControlSphere",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A pull_request_target workflow checks out the pull request head, running untrusted code with repository secrets and a write token."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A pull_request_target workflow checks out the pull request head, running untrusted code with repository secrets and a write token. The build or runtime executes code from a source outside the trust boundary, such as an untrusted pull request in a privileged CI workflow or an unpinned third-party action."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Bind request data only to an explicit allow-list of fields (DTOs), never merge untrusted objects into prototypes or configuration, and load code and libraries only from fixed, trusted locations.\n\nSeparate untrusted builds from privileged jobs and review CI configuration as code.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Bind request data only to an explicit allow-list of fields (DTOs), never merge untrusted objects into prototypes or configuration, and load code and libraries only from fixed, trusted locations.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Separate untrusted builds from privileged jobs and review CI configuration as code."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/829.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-829",
                  "OWASP-A08:2021",
                  "security"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.3",
                "precision": "high"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "CWE-829",
                    "index": 29,
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "index": 0
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "superset"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "iac.k8s.privileged",
              "name": "ExecutionWithUnnecessaryPrivileges",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container 'api' is privileged."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Container 'api' is privileged. A process, container or job runs with more privileges than its function requires, for example as root or with a privileged container flag."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Ship secure defaults: disable debug mode in production, set Secure, HttpOnly and SameSite on session cookies, expire sessions, verify TLS certificates, and restrict CORS to the origins that need it.\n\nEnforce least privilege with admission policies (for example Pod Security Standards) and image linting in CI.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Ship secure defaults: disable debug mode in production, set Secure, HttpOnly and SameSite on session cookies, expire sessions, verify TLS certificates, and restrict CORS to the origins that need it.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Enforce least privilege with admission policies (for example Pod Security Standards) and image linting in CI."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/250.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-250",
                  "OWASP-A05:2021",
                  "security"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.3",
                "precision": "high"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "CWE-250",
                    "index": 8,
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "index": 0
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "superset"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "taint.http_param.sql",
              "name": "SqlInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data from a http_param source reaches a sql sink (cur.execute)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Data from a http_param source reaches a sql sink (cur.execute). A database query is built by concatenating or interpolating data that an external party controls, so that data is parsed as SQL rather than treated as a value."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "If account_id can be attacker-controlled, use the database driver's parameter-binding API and pass account_id separately from the SQL text, without quoting the placeholder. Optionally enforce the expected identifier type as defense in depth.\n\nStandardise on an ORM or query builder that parameterises by default, restrict the database account to the least privilege required, and add query-construction checks to code review and CI.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** If account_id can be attacker-controlled, use the database driver's parameter-binding API and pass account_id separately from the SQL text, without quoting the placeholder. Optionally enforce the expected identifier type as defense in depth.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Standardise on an ORM or query builder that parameterises by default, restrict the database account to the least privilege required, and add query-construction checks to code review and CI."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-89",
                  "OWASP-A03:2021",
                  "security"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.3",
                "precision": "high"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "CWE-89",
                    "index": 5,
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "index": 0
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "superset"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "secret.connection_string",
              "name": "UseOfHardCodedCredentials",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hard-coded credential of type connection_string (masked preview po****** (51 chars), entropy 4.91 bits/char)."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hard-coded credential of type connection_string (masked preview po****** (51 chars), entropy 4.91 bits/char). A credential such as a password, API key or token is embedded in the source code."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Remove the credential from source code and version history, rotate it immediately, and load secrets at run time from a secrets manager or the environment. Add secret scanning to the pre-commit hooks and CI so a new secret is caught before it is pushed.\n\nAdopt a secret manager, add pre-commit and CI secret scanning, and purge the value from version-control history.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Remove the credential from source code and version history, rotate it immediately, and load secrets at run time from a secrets manager or the environment. Add secret scanning to the pre-commit hooks and CI so a new secret is caught before it is pushed.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Adopt a secret manager, add pre-commit and CI secret scanning, and purge the value from version-control history."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-798",
