            {
              "id": "secret.private_key_block",
              "name": "UseOfHardCodedCredentials",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hard-coded credential of type private_key_block (masked preview --****** (313 chars), entropy 5.97 bits/char)."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hard-coded credential of type private_key_block (masked preview --****** (313 chars), entropy 5.97 bits/char). A credential such as a password, API key or token is embedded in the source code."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Remove the credential from source code and version history, rotate it immediately, and load secrets at run time from a secrets manager or the environment. Add secret scanning to the pre-commit hooks and CI so a new secret is caught before it is pushed.\n\nAdopt a secret manager, add pre-commit and CI secret scanning, and purge the value from version-control history.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Remove the credential from source code and version history, rotate it immediately, and load secrets at run time from a secrets manager or the environment. Add secret scanning to the pre-commit hooks and CI so a new secret is caught before it is pushed.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Adopt a secret manager, add pre-commit and CI secret scanning, and purge the value from version-control history."
