            {
              "id": "py.insecure-deserialisation",
              "name": "DeserialisationOfUntrustedData",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data is deserialised with a loader that can construct arbitrary objects."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Data is deserialised with a loader that can construct arbitrary objects. Data from outside the trust boundary is deserialised with a loader that can instantiate arbitrary types or invoke code during loading."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "If blob can be untrusted, replace pickle with a non-executable format such as JSON plus strict schema validation. If pickle is unavoidable, accept it only from a trusted source and verify a cryptographic signature before calling pickle.loads.\n\nAdopt data-only formats with schema validation at trust boundaries, and sign serialised objects that must round-trip through clients.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** If blob can be untrusted, replace pickle with a non-executable format such as JSON plus strict schema validation. If pickle is unavoidable, accept it only from a trusted source and verify a cryptographic signature before calling pickle.loads.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Adopt data-only formats with schema validation at trust boundaries, and sign serialised objects that must round-trip through clients."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
