            {
              "id": "sca.vulnerable-dependency",
              "name": "DependencyOnVulnerableThirdPartyComponent",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Vulnerable dependency: PyYAML 5.3 (CVE-2020-14343)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vulnerable dependency: PyYAML 5.3 (CVE-2020-14343)\n- GHSA-8q59-q68h-6hv4 (CVE-2020-14343), critical: PyYAML arbitrary code execution when loading untrusted YAML with the full loader. Fixed in 5.4.\nRemediation: upgrade PyYAML to 5.4 or later (resolves all listed advisories).\nReachability: no import of the package was found in the scanned code; it may be a transitive or unused dependency.\nExploitation data: no KEV or EPSS snapshot installed (run `codekavach sca update`)."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Bind request data only to an explicit allow-list of fields (DTOs), never merge untrusted objects into prototypes or configuration, and load code and libraries only from fixed, trusted locations.\n\nRun software composition analysis in CI, keep an SBOM, and automate dependency updates.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Bind request data only to an explicit allow-list of fields (DTOs), never merge untrusted objects into prototypes or configuration, and load code and libraries only from fixed, trusted locations.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Run software composition analysis in CI, keep an SBOM, and automate dependency updates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1395.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-1395",
