            {
              "id": "iac.actions.script-injection",
              "name": "OsCommandInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A run step in job 'build' interpolates attacker-controlled event data into a shell script; pass it through an environment variable instead."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A run step in job 'build' interpolates attacker-controlled event data into a shell script; pass it through an environment variable instead. The application builds an operating-system command from data that an external party can influence and runs it through a shell. Shell metacharacters in that data change the command that is executed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Do not build commands, code or templates from untrusted input. Call the program directly with an argument list (for example subprocess.run([...], shell=False)) instead of a shell string, never pass request data to eval/exec or a template compiler, and validate input against a strict allow-list of expected values before it reaches the sink.\n\nReplace shell invocations with native library calls where possible, run the service with least privilege, and add a static-analysis gate that blocks shell=True and string-built commands.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Do not build commands, code or templates from untrusted input. Call the program directly with an argument list (for example subprocess.run([...], shell=False)) instead of a shell string, never pass request data to eval/exec or a template compiler, and validate input against a strict allow-list of expected values before it reaches the sink.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Replace shell invocations with native library calls where possible, run the service with least privilege, and add a static-analysis gate that blocks shell=True and string-built commands."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-78",
