            {
              "id": "iac.terraform.s3-public-acl",
              "name": "IncorrectPermissionAssignmentForCriticalResource",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket 'statements' uses a public ACL."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket 'statements' uses a public ACL. A critical resource is readable or writable by principals that should not have access."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Enforce authorisation on the server for every request: check that the authenticated principal owns or may act on the referenced object (deny by default), derive the owner from the session rather than from request parameters, and centralise the check in a decorator or policy layer so no handler can skip it.\n\nAudit permissions in CI and use least-privilege defaults.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Enforce authorisation on the server for every request: check that the authenticated principal owns or may act on the referenced object (deny by default), derive the owner from the session rather than from request parameters, and centralise the check in a decorator or policy layer so no handler can skip it.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Audit permissions in CI and use least-privilege defaults."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/732.html",
