            {
              "id": "iac.appconfig.tls-verification-disabled",
              "name": "ImproperCertificateValidation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "TLS certificate verification is disabled, enabling man-in-the-middle attacks."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "TLS certificate verification is disabled, enabling man-in-the-middle attacks. TLS certificate validation is disabled or incomplete."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use current, vetted primitives from a maintained library: AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 for encryption with a fresh random nonce per message, SHA-256 or better for integrity, a password hashing function (Argon2id, scrypt, bcrypt) for passwords, and the operating system CSPRNG (Python secrets / os.urandom) for keys, tokens and IVs.\n\nPin trust stores centrally and forbid verify=False in CI.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Use current, vetted primitives from a maintained library: AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 for encryption with a fresh random nonce per message, SHA-256 or better for integrity, a password hashing function (Argon2id, scrypt, bcrypt) for passwords, and the operating system CSPRNG (Python secrets / os.urandom) for keys, tokens and IVs.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Pin trust stores centrally and forbid verify=False in CI."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/295.html",
