            {
              "id": "iac.appconfig.weak-tls-version",
              "name": "InadequateEncryptionStrength",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A deprecated protocol version (SSLv2/3, TLS 1.0 or 1.1) is allowed."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A deprecated protocol version (SSLv2/3, TLS 1.0 or 1.1) is allowed. Encryption uses a key size or algorithm strength below current recommendations."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use current, vetted primitives from a maintained library: AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 for encryption with a fresh random nonce per message, SHA-256 or better for integrity, a password hashing function (Argon2id, scrypt, bcrypt) for passwords, and the operating system CSPRNG (Python secrets / os.urandom) for keys, tokens and IVs.\n\nMaintain an approved-algorithms list enforced in CI.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Use current, vetted primitives from a maintained library: AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 for encryption with a fresh random nonce per message, SHA-256 or better for integrity, a password hashing function (Argon2id, scrypt, bcrypt) for passwords, and the operating system CSPRNG (Python secrets / os.urandom) for keys, tokens and IVs.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Maintain an approved-algorithms list enforced in CI."
