            {
              "id": "taint.http_param.path",
              "name": "PathTraversal",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data from a http_param source reaches a path sink (fs.createReadStream)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Data from a http_param source reaches a path sink (fs.createReadStream). A file-system path is built from data an external party controls without checking that the resolved path stays inside the intended directory."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Prefer mapping an allowlisted identifier to a server-controlled filename. Otherwise, canonicalize both config.exportDir and the requested file, reject absolute or traversal paths, verify the canonical result remains beneath the canonical base directory, and account for symlink escapes.\n\nCentralise file access behind a storage service that enforces containment, and run the process with a file-system view restricted to the data it needs.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Prefer mapping an allowlisted identifier to a server-controlled filename. Otherwise, canonicalize both config.exportDir and the requested file, reject absolute or traversal paths, verify the canonical result remains beneath the canonical base directory, and account for symlink escapes.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Centralise file access behind a storage service that enforces containment, and run the process with a file-system view restricted to the data it needs."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
