            {
              "id": "py.insecure-direct-object-reference",
              "name": "AuthorisationBypassThroughUserControlledKeyIdor",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A record is fetched by an identifier from the caller with no ownership check."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A record is fetched by an identifier from the caller with no ownership check. A record is retrieved by an identifier supplied by the caller without verifying that the caller is entitled to that record."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Enforce authorisation on the server for every request: check that the authenticated principal owns or may act on the referenced object (deny by default), derive the owner from the session rather than from request parameters, and centralise the check in a decorator or policy layer so no handler can skip it.\n\nEnforce object-level authorisation in a shared data-access layer and add negative authorisation tests for every resource endpoint.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Enforce authorisation on the server for every request: check that the authenticated principal owns or may act on the referenced object (deny by default), derive the owner from the session rather than from request parameters, and centralise the check in a decorator or policy layer so no handler can skip it.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Enforce object-level authorisation in a shared data-access layer and add negative authorisation tests for every resource endpoint."
              },
