            {
              "id": "py.missing-authorization",
              "name": "MissingAuthorisation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "An account-scoped route has no authentication or authorisation check."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An account-scoped route has no authentication or authorisation check. A route that acts on protected resources performs no authentication or authorisation check before doing so."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Enforce authorisation on the server for every request: check that the authenticated principal owns or may act on the referenced object (deny by default), derive the owner from the session rather than from request parameters, and centralise the check in a decorator or policy layer so no handler can skip it.\n\nMake authorisation deny-by-default at the framework level so a new route is protected unless explicitly opened, and test it in CI.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Enforce authorisation on the server for every request: check that the authenticated principal owns or may act on the referenced object (deny by default), derive the owner from the session rather than from request parameters, and centralise the check in a decorator or policy layer so no handler can skip it.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Make authorisation deny-by-default at the framework level so a new route is protected unless explicitly opened, and test it in CI."
