            {
              "id": "py.weak-password-hash",
              "name": "UseOfABrokenOrRiskyCryptographicAlgorithm",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A password is hashed with an algorithm that is broken or far too fast."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A password is hashed with an algorithm that is broken or far too fast. The code relies on a cryptographic algorithm that is broken or unsuitable for its purpose, such as MD5 or SHA-1 for password storage."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use current, vetted primitives from a maintained library: AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 for encryption with a fresh random nonce per message, SHA-256 or better for integrity, a password hashing function (Argon2id, scrypt, bcrypt) for passwords, and the operating system CSPRNG (Python secrets / os.urandom) for keys, tokens and IVs.\n\nMaintain an approved-algorithms list, wrap cryptography in a small vetted internal library, and add a CI check that rejects deprecated primitives.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Use current, vetted primitives from a maintained library: AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305 for encryption with a fresh random nonce per message, SHA-256 or better for integrity, a password hashing function (Argon2id, scrypt, bcrypt) for passwords, and the operating system CSPRNG (Python secrets / os.urandom) for keys, tokens and IVs.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Maintain an approved-algorithms list, wrap cryptography in a small vetted internal library, and add a CI check that rejects deprecated primitives."
              },
