            {
              "id": "py.static-iv",
              "name": "PredictableInitialisationVector",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A block cipher is given a fixed initialisation vector instead of a random one."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A block cipher is given a fixed initialisation vector instead of a random one. A block cipher in a chaining mode is used with a fixed or predictable initialisation vector."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "If STATIC_IV is reused or predictable, generate a fresh cryptographically random 16-byte IV for every encryption and store or transmit it with the ciphertext; preferably use an authenticated-encryption mode such as AES-GCM with correct nonce uniqueness.\n\nMove to an authenticated encryption mode such as AES-GCM through a vetted library that manages nonces for you.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** If STATIC_IV is reused or predictable, generate a fresh cryptographically random 16-byte IV for every encryption and store or transmit it with the ciphertext; preferably use an authenticated-encryption mode such as AES-GCM with correct nonce uniqueness.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Move to an authenticated encryption mode such as AES-GCM through a vetted library that manages nonces for you."
              },
