            {
              "id": "iac.k8s.no-limits",
              "name": "AllocationOfResourcesWithoutLimits",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container 'api' has no resource limits."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Container 'api' has no resource limits. A resource such as memory, connections or request size is allocated without a limit."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Bound every resource an attacker can drive: limit request and upload sizes, decompressed archive sizes and entry counts, use regular expressions without nested quantifiers (or a linear-time engine) on untrusted input, and set time-outs and rate limits.\n\nAdopt rate limiting and resource quotas as platform defaults.",
                "markdown": "**Fix now.** Bound every resource an attacker can drive: limit request and upload sizes, decompressed archive sizes and entry counts, use regular expressions without nested quantifiers (or a linear-time engine) on untrusted input, and set time-outs and rate limits.\n\n**Prevent recurrence.** Adopt rate limiting and resource quotas as platform defaults."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
